WEBVTT

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:04.850
<i>For generations, House Ingram 
has guarded the royal family</i>

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:06.610
<i>and protected the country.</i>

00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:16.650
You've improved quite a bit, Harold.

00:00:16.650 --> 00:00:18.830
Shall we call it a day?

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:20.870
Grand Master Ingram,

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:23.770
would you join us for dinner tonight?

00:00:23.770 --> 00:00:26.460
My wife has been wanting to see Joshua.

00:00:26.810 --> 00:00:30.650
Then we'll settle this the usual way: 
with a drinking contest!

00:00:31.790 --> 00:00:33.220
Bring it on!

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:39.090
<i>After Mom passed, Dad raised me by himself.</i>

00:00:40.030 --> 00:00:40.880
<i>But...</i>

00:00:56.680 --> 00:00:57.540
Joshua.

00:00:58.030 --> 00:01:02.240
Your father served nobly
 right up to the end.

00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:12.990
It appears Princess Yuki is fond of you.

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:19.760
You will live in the Royal Palace 
of Soleil from now on.

00:01:20.310 --> 00:01:22.390
You must make Princess Yuki smile.

00:01:22.830 --> 00:01:23.770
We're counting on you.

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:26.680
<i>As my father's son,</i>

00:01:26.680 --> 00:01:28.490
<i>as a man of House Ingram,</i>

00:01:29.110 --> 00:01:32.330
<i>I swore that I would protect her smile.</i>

00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:36.200
Let's go.

00:01:36.520 --> 00:01:38.180
<i>We're arriving in the theater of operations.</i>

00:01:38.180 --> 00:01:39.460
<i>All units deploy.</i>

00:02:02.530 --> 00:02:04.730
Dracorn Unit, Monocherous Unit, 
take the right wing.

00:02:04.730 --> 00:02:07.170
Gigarth Unit, Fantazma Unit, 
take the left wing and fan out.

00:02:07.170 --> 00:02:08.550
Dracorn, roger that.

00:02:08.550 --> 00:02:09.620
Monocherous, roger that.

00:02:09.620 --> 00:02:10.710
Gigarth, roger that.

00:02:10.710 --> 00:02:11.770
Fantazma, roger that.

00:02:11.770 --> 00:02:16.030
Pegasus Unit, vanguard. Lead the Chranio 
and Larva Units with the Margrave's Unit

00:02:16.030 --> 00:02:17.760
to set up a defense line 
at the designated point.

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:19.820
Testa Unit, cover the carrier.

00:02:19.820 --> 00:02:21.160
Pegasus, roger that.

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:22.330
Testa, roger that.

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:27.830
Deploying fifteen-car infantry 
company to act as reserves.

00:02:38.540 --> 00:02:40.230
Reporting five enemy carriers.

00:02:40.230 --> 00:02:43.140
We believe it to be 
the Imperial 8th Area Army.

00:02:45.530 --> 00:02:49.560
There's no place more crucial to 
national defense than northern Wister.

00:02:50.070 --> 00:02:54.820
This is the only route by which the Empire 
can mount a land invasion on a massive scale.

00:02:55.610 --> 00:03:00.170
The large canyons throughout the wasteland
 provide a natural stronghold,

00:03:00.170 --> 00:03:02.660
so the enemy has merely been 
biding their time until now.

00:03:03.020 --> 00:03:04.480
If they manage to break through,

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:07.140
the war will spread quickly 
throughout the kingdom.

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:08.410
We're at a critical moment.

00:03:08.410 --> 00:03:10.160
Main cannons, fire!

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:18.240
Keep calm.

00:03:18.730 --> 00:03:20.650
Just do it like in training.

00:03:20.650 --> 00:03:22.970
Stay strong, Joshua Ingram!

00:03:37.070 --> 00:03:39.110
The Price of Smiles

00:03:37.070 --> 00:03:39.110
<i>The Price of Smiles</i>

00:04:53.730 --> 00:04:59.400
<b><i>The Truth of the War</i></b>

00:04:55.040 --> 00:04:56.940
Joshua's not picking up!

00:04:57.300 --> 00:04:58.700
Of course he isn't.

00:04:58.700 --> 00:05:03.940
It's about time for the talks between 
the Royal Order and the Empire to begin.

00:05:04.260 --> 00:05:06.250
The State of Wister, huh?

00:05:06.250 --> 00:05:07.700
It's so far away...

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:11.740
I wonder if Joshua's okay.

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:15.210
I hope he hasn't made their Order angry...

00:05:16.330 --> 00:05:21.280
Unlike us, the Empire of Grandiga 
does not practice chivalry.

00:05:21.280 --> 00:05:23.640
Thus, they lack a chivalric order.

00:05:23.640 --> 00:05:25.470
What? Really?

00:05:25.940 --> 00:05:26.590
Yes.

00:05:26.980 --> 00:05:29.570
A state in which the military elite 
hold the authority over the citizenry,

00:05:29.570 --> 00:05:31.160
a military dictatorship.

00:05:31.470 --> 00:05:35.140
That is the nature of the force 
with which we share this planet,

00:05:35.140 --> 00:05:36.640
the Grandiga Empire.

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:37.840
Prepare for close combat!

00:05:37.840 --> 00:05:39.040
Don't let them get through!

00:06:11.610 --> 00:06:12.570
What's wrong?

00:06:12.570 --> 00:06:14.220
Wound up about your first live combat?

00:06:14.220 --> 00:06:15.560
Commander...

00:06:15.560 --> 00:06:17.090
I'll watch your six.

00:06:17.090 --> 00:06:18.980
Go out there and show 'em
 what you can do!

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:21.730
Roger that!

00:06:21.730 --> 00:06:22.450
Let's go!

00:06:22.450 --> 00:06:25.990
Passion and will!

00:06:32.970 --> 00:06:34.100
Not bad.

00:06:34.100 --> 00:06:36.410
Never knew a Gard could move like that.

00:06:36.410 --> 00:06:38.300
Our right wing, Dracorn and Monocherous Units

00:06:38.300 --> 00:06:40.080
have gotten to within 800 of enemy fleet.

00:06:43.040 --> 00:06:44.420
Assembly line trash!

00:06:44.680 --> 00:06:45.630
They're nothing!

00:06:52.540 --> 00:06:54.600
Enemy forces are withdrawing!

00:06:54.600 --> 00:06:56.330
Too easy.

00:06:56.750 --> 00:07:00.830
This was a recon operation 
to determine our strength.

00:07:00.830 --> 00:07:02.600
I know that, James.

00:07:02.840 --> 00:07:05.610
But we haven't revealed 
our trump card yet, either.

00:07:07.260 --> 00:07:08.380
Withdraw!

00:07:08.380 --> 00:07:10.360
All units, hurry back to the ships!

00:07:21.940 --> 00:07:24.580
I'm still alive, Yuki.

00:07:24.580 --> 00:07:25.920
Oh?

00:07:26.090 --> 00:07:27.980
Is that supposed to be Princess Yuki?

00:07:27.980 --> 00:07:30.550
You've got a real precious side, you know.

00:07:32.240 --> 00:07:34.340
Are you still keeping it from the princess?

00:07:34.660 --> 00:07:38.310
The fact that war has broken out 
between us and the Empire...

00:07:38.310 --> 00:07:39.290
Yeah.

00:07:39.290 --> 00:07:43.310
I can't imagine how sad 
she'd be to learn about it.

00:07:43.690 --> 00:07:47.320
I hope she never has to know, 
so that she can just keep smiling.

00:07:49.510 --> 00:07:52.590
Yuki will always be a symbol 
of peace for our kingdom.

00:07:52.980 --> 00:07:55.820
Keeping her from harm is 
our duty as retainers.

00:07:57.050 --> 00:07:57.930
Understood.

00:07:58.340 --> 00:08:00.830
We must hold the enemy off here.

00:08:02.050 --> 00:08:03.620
I look forward to working with you.

00:08:03.620 --> 00:08:06.840
It's time to really show 
our passion and will!

00:08:07.170 --> 00:08:10.610
Sorry. We're not big on the fiery rhetoric.

00:08:11.160 --> 00:08:13.530
I really wish you'd stop shouting it 
over the comms, too.

00:08:13.530 --> 00:08:15.490
It gives me a headache.

00:08:15.490 --> 00:08:17.150
S-Sorry...

00:08:18.130 --> 00:08:21.300
This is the signal from Grad, 
capital of the State of Wister, to enter port.

00:08:21.300 --> 00:08:22.640
The gate will now open.

00:08:38.690 --> 00:08:39.990
That's our lord,

00:08:40.630 --> 00:08:42.500
Margrave Girard.

00:08:42.980 --> 00:08:45.550
The situation seems to have deteriorated.

00:08:45.550 --> 00:08:46.420
Yes.

00:08:46.980 --> 00:08:51.260
Our active forces have dropped 
to almost 30% of where they were

00:08:51.660 --> 00:08:54.760
when you and the twins left 
for Hariant ten days ago.

00:08:55.220 --> 00:08:59.060
But we're glad to get that 
new chrars you brought.

00:08:59.060 --> 00:09:02.020
Yuni, Lune, I'm glad you're both safe, as well.

00:09:02.800 --> 00:09:03.820
Yes, sir.

00:09:03.820 --> 00:09:05.270
We're unworthy of your praise.

00:09:05.920 --> 00:09:07.270
I'm counting on you.

00:09:11.830 --> 00:09:14.280
If I might offer a piece of advice...

00:09:14.810 --> 00:09:16.650
We don't have any time to lose.

00:09:16.650 --> 00:09:18.910
I believe it's time to bring out our trump card.

00:09:20.140 --> 00:09:21.660
What do you mean?

00:09:21.970 --> 00:09:23.300
Keep it moving forward!

00:09:23.300 --> 00:09:24.540
Don't jostle it!

00:09:24.830 --> 00:09:26.740
Stop! Lower it in!

00:09:29.800 --> 00:09:32.090
Installation complete! Connection confirmed!

00:09:32.580 --> 00:09:34.660
Is that the new chrars?

00:09:41.670 --> 00:09:43.100
I'm increasing the output!

00:09:48.580 --> 00:09:50.560
He really is reckless.

00:09:50.560 --> 00:09:54.690
Altitude is 70... 75 over 
chrars stability level.

00:09:54.960 --> 00:09:57.450
Is he trying to break the altitude barrier?

00:09:57.700 --> 00:10:00.440
It was one thing for the technology 
of the ancient immigrants,

00:10:00.440 --> 00:10:04.200
but these days, operating an air 
force on this planet is impossible.

00:10:04.430 --> 00:10:07.710
The chrars stops responding 
and you can't produce energy.

00:10:07.950 --> 00:10:10.700
One hundred. Altitude barrier broken.

00:10:15.010 --> 00:10:16.960
I-It's no use...

00:10:16.960 --> 00:10:18.090
Is that the limit?

00:10:18.620 --> 00:10:20.550
Go!

00:10:25.300 --> 00:10:26.560
Did you see that power?

00:10:26.560 --> 00:10:27.690
Impossible!

00:10:27.930 --> 00:10:30.190
So it still won't get us to flight.

00:10:30.500 --> 00:10:34.980
But if we could power our entire 
army with this new chrars...

00:10:37.740 --> 00:10:41.960
I'll install the remaining two 
new chrars into your theurgears.

00:10:43.190 --> 00:10:45.430
Tomorrow, we'll make the first strike.

00:10:45.430 --> 00:10:47.080
We're going to get a few licks in, too.

00:10:49.560 --> 00:10:50.910
We can do this.

00:10:50.910 --> 00:10:53.170
With power like this, 
we have nothing to fear.

00:11:00.290 --> 00:11:03.100
<i>It's bad for your health to 
stay up this late, Princess.</i>

00:11:03.410 --> 00:11:04.550
Joshua!

00:11:08.210 --> 00:11:11.040
Plant them on the hovers and the limb joints.

00:11:11.040 --> 00:11:12.700
We just need to ground them.

00:11:19.700 --> 00:11:21.610
No luck, huh?

00:11:22.910 --> 00:11:28.000
I heard our ancestors' planet was 
covered in beautiful flowers, though...

00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:31.190
<i>Maybe sunflowers just won't 
bloom on this planet.</i>

00:11:32.250 --> 00:11:35.930
<i>I wonder why... Maybe the soil 
just isn't right for them?</i>

00:11:35.930 --> 00:11:37.250
I don't know.

00:11:37.440 --> 00:11:39.800
But Izana told me...

00:11:39.800 --> 00:11:45.010
When Mother was alive, she worked hard 
trying to get these flowers to grow.

00:11:46.120 --> 00:11:47.140
<i>I hear you.</i>

00:11:47.140 --> 00:11:49.020
<i>I'll look into it, too.</i>

00:11:50.080 --> 00:11:51.190
Really?

00:11:51.190 --> 00:11:53.320
<i>Well, I should go. Early day tomorrow.</i>

00:11:53.800 --> 00:11:55.240
<i>I'll call you again soon.</i>

00:11:55.240 --> 00:11:56.170
Sure!

00:11:56.170 --> 00:11:58.280
Good luck with your duties, Joshua!

00:11:58.480 --> 00:11:59.320
<i>Right.</i>

00:11:59.320 --> 00:12:01.060
<i>Good night, Yuki.</i>

00:12:01.060 --> 00:12:02.620
<i>Pleasant dreams.</i>

00:12:09.660 --> 00:12:13.670
<i>That Joshua... Has he matured 
some since last I saw him?</i>

00:12:13.970 --> 00:12:16.830
Princess Yuki, you haven't moved.

00:12:16.830 --> 00:12:18.500
R-Right.

00:12:24.030 --> 00:12:25.420
That's checkmate!

00:12:25.420 --> 00:12:27.000
That's against the rules.

00:12:27.000 --> 00:12:30.930
But in a real battle, people don't 
always play by the rules, do they?

00:12:31.150 --> 00:12:33.990
That mock battle before was so much fun!

00:12:33.990 --> 00:12:37.230
I think I might actually be 
pretty good at that stuff!

00:12:37.230 --> 00:12:39.160
Can I do it again some time?

00:12:39.160 --> 00:12:42.110
Using a theurgear is a lot 
more fun than chess!

00:12:43.060 --> 00:12:46.040
War is not a game.

00:12:46.040 --> 00:12:47.370
Never forget that.

00:12:48.680 --> 00:12:49.920
Well, of course it's not.

00:12:49.920 --> 00:12:51.790
Even I know that!

00:12:52.240 --> 00:12:53.980
You're weird, Miss Layla.

00:12:55.940 --> 00:12:57.540
Did you send the request for a ceasefire?

00:12:57.810 --> 00:12:58.960
I did.

00:12:58.960 --> 00:13:00.300
But there was no response.

00:13:02.160 --> 00:13:04.460
The Empire's territory is vast,

00:13:04.460 --> 00:13:08.400
but they don't have 
the resources to maintain it all.

00:13:08.400 --> 00:13:10.830
It was obvious that they would try to invade.

00:13:10.830 --> 00:13:15.800
To oppose them, we rushed 
the development of new chrars, but...

00:13:15.800 --> 00:13:17.560
It backfired?

00:13:18.890 --> 00:13:24.190
The empire was waiting for us 
to complete the new chrars.

00:13:24.190 --> 00:13:27.320
They chose to invade now 
in order to steal it.

00:13:27.580 --> 00:13:30.560
It's pointless to debate about it now.

00:13:30.560 --> 00:13:33.080
Our kingdom's future was 
already far from bright.

00:13:33.360 --> 00:13:36.460
You were aware of that, too, 
weren't you, Layla?

00:13:37.760 --> 00:13:42.090
Every year, our country's soil 
produces lower crop yields.

00:13:42.390 --> 00:13:44.060
It wasn't just about boosting our military.

00:13:44.060 --> 00:13:48.630
We needed the new chrars to keep 
the people from starvation.

00:13:50.280 --> 00:13:52.930
The Empire has materiel superiority.

00:13:52.930 --> 00:13:56.050
But our individual machines have 
superior specs and armaments.

00:13:56.050 --> 00:13:56.970
Therefore...

00:13:57.630 --> 00:13:59.360
Rather than continuing this war of attrition,

00:13:59.360 --> 00:14:02.860
we need to stretch out the front 
and whittle down the enemy forces.

00:14:03.240 --> 00:14:05.150
This will be the main theater.

00:14:05.150 --> 00:14:06.830
Six platoons, including Pegasus,

00:14:06.830 --> 00:14:09.240
and the Margrave's unit will set an ambush,

00:14:09.620 --> 00:14:12.260
while another unit leads
 the enemy to them.

00:14:12.260 --> 00:14:14.870
Joshua, that will be your 
Gard's responsibility.

00:14:16.130 --> 00:14:17.120
Yes, sir!

00:14:17.880 --> 00:14:20.580
Just to be safe, Dracorn Unit, 
Monocheros Unit,

00:14:20.580 --> 00:14:22.500
you'll stand watch over this tributary tunnel

00:14:22.870 --> 00:14:23.930
Yes, sir!

00:14:23.930 --> 00:14:25.760
Plant explosives on either end.

00:14:25.960 --> 00:14:28.450
If we have to, we'll collapse the ravine

00:14:28.450 --> 00:14:30.510
and seal off their route into Grad.

00:14:31.930 --> 00:14:33.920
We'll commence the operation in 90 minutes.

00:14:34.260 --> 00:14:35.770
All soldiers, take your positions!

00:14:36.350 --> 00:14:37.270
Yes, sir!

00:15:00.980 --> 00:15:02.760
Pegasus 2, safe and sound!

00:15:02.760 --> 00:15:03.690
Great job!

00:15:03.690 --> 00:15:05.130
Krivanovs, fire at will!

00:15:28.180 --> 00:15:32.450
If you're trying to trigger the explosives 
planted on the three theurgears yesterday,

00:15:32.450 --> 00:15:33.960
we've already removed them.

00:15:35.230 --> 00:15:40.250
Using the new chrars as a bargaining chip 
to negotiate a surrender to the Empire...

00:15:40.250 --> 00:15:41.460
Was that the plan?

00:15:41.850 --> 00:15:42.960
Why did you betray us?

00:15:44.070 --> 00:15:47.480
The fighting over these last 
ten days has made it clear...

00:15:47.480 --> 00:15:50.030
The empire is more serious 
than it's ever been.

00:15:50.030 --> 00:15:54.220
The new chrars are impressive, 
but three alone won't save us.

00:15:54.770 --> 00:15:57.420
I didn't want to see my city 
burned to the ground.

00:15:57.740 --> 00:16:02.980
I was willing to face the disgrace of 
betrayal to keep my people alive.

00:16:03.270 --> 00:16:04.300
Fool.

00:16:05.400 --> 00:16:09.740
With a mindset so preoccupied with peace, 
you'll never protect anything.

00:16:10.220 --> 00:16:12.740
Lord Girard... why?

00:16:13.250 --> 00:16:15.430
I'll keep Grad safe if it costs me my life.

00:16:16.020 --> 00:16:19.120
On that, I will stake my pride 
as a knight of this region!

00:16:30.860 --> 00:16:31.470
What?!

00:16:31.880 --> 00:16:34.040
Damned Empire! 
They've got tactics like this?!

00:16:47.430 --> 00:16:49.410
This is Gigarth 3!

00:16:49.410 --> 00:16:51.640
The Krivanovs have suffered major losses!

00:16:54.720 --> 00:16:56.230
Seal off all routes!

00:16:56.230 --> 00:16:58.090
All units, return to Grad.

00:16:58.090 --> 00:16:59.870
Prepare for a siege!

00:16:59.870 --> 00:17:01.140
Roger that!

00:17:13.970 --> 00:17:15.840
Route A sealed!

00:17:26.800 --> 00:17:27.900
It won't trigger!

00:17:28.810 --> 00:17:30.480
Enemy squad sighted!

00:17:30.480 --> 00:17:31.800
Fall back!

00:17:33.510 --> 00:17:35.700
Dracorn, Monocheros, switch to defense!

00:17:35.700 --> 00:17:37.450
We don't know how many of them there are!

00:17:37.450 --> 00:17:38.620
Yuni!

00:17:38.620 --> 00:17:39.910
Damn. My machine's locked up!

00:17:40.250 --> 00:17:41.660
Lune! I'll go!

00:17:49.590 --> 00:17:51.050
I'll detonate it directly!

00:17:51.340 --> 00:17:52.340
We'll back you up!

00:17:58.430 --> 00:18:00.260
Don't get in my way!

00:18:03.140 --> 00:18:04.980
Damn it!

00:18:08.730 --> 00:18:09.490
Joshua?

00:18:09.490 --> 00:18:10.980
I'll handle it! Get out of here!

00:18:14.400 --> 00:18:17.110
Passion and will!

00:18:19.710 --> 00:18:20.870
Is this as far as I go?

00:18:22.350 --> 00:18:25.620
But I won't let you people 
get any further, either!

00:18:26.800 --> 00:18:28.670
So long, Yuki!

00:18:39.800 --> 00:18:40.760
Turn off your engine!

00:18:40.760 --> 00:18:42.050
We're getting out of here!

00:18:43.170 --> 00:18:44.600
I appreciate what you did.

00:18:45.500 --> 00:18:47.560
I suppose I'm in your debt...

00:18:48.120 --> 00:18:50.560
You've got a real precious side, you know?

00:18:51.640 --> 00:18:54.070
Sh-Shut up!

00:18:57.920 --> 00:18:59.820
I didn't quite manage to die...

00:18:59.820 --> 00:19:02.920
But then, I'm not really the hero type, am I?

00:19:03.310 --> 00:19:04.080
But...

00:19:05.490 --> 00:19:07.730
Watch me, Dad.

00:19:07.730 --> 00:19:11.030
I'm going to surpass you!

00:19:17.150 --> 00:19:18.560
I did it!

00:19:18.960 --> 00:19:20.550
I know! I should tell Joshua!

00:19:20.550 --> 00:19:21.560
Princess Yuki.

00:19:22.550 --> 00:19:24.170
Prepare to depart.

00:19:25.260 --> 00:19:26.970
What's wrong, Miss Layla?

00:19:27.510 --> 00:19:30.050
I'll explain later. Just come along.

00:19:30.050 --> 00:19:31.480
Okay, but where are we going?

00:19:31.860 --> 00:19:34.820
To Meredith, capital of the State of Soleil.

00:19:34.820 --> 00:19:37.170
The Order's carrier is pulling into port.

00:19:37.890 --> 00:19:39.240
Will Joshua be with them?

00:19:39.240 --> 00:19:40.900
I'm so glad!

00:19:40.900 --> 00:19:43.120
There's something I have to tell him,

00:19:43.440 --> 00:19:45.620
but I can't seem to get in 
touch with him by terminal!

00:19:46.290 --> 00:19:47.650
I'm so happy, though!

00:19:47.650 --> 00:19:51.310
It's been years since I last left Hariant!

00:19:55.570 --> 00:19:57.000
The Order's carrier...

00:19:57.350 --> 00:19:58.520
What happened?

00:19:58.520 --> 00:20:00.600
After a five-day siege,

00:20:00.600 --> 00:20:04.440
a border city called Grad 
fell into enemy hands.

00:20:05.690 --> 00:20:07.920
Margrave Girard surrendered.

00:20:08.230 --> 00:20:11.230
The Order narrowly managed 
to escape and came here.

00:20:11.690 --> 00:20:13.770
What are you guys talking about?

00:20:14.530 --> 00:20:15.700
What's going on?

00:20:15.700 --> 00:20:17.020
That theurgear before...

00:20:17.510 --> 00:20:19.320
Why was it... so...

00:20:30.480 --> 00:20:31.660
I'm sorry.

00:20:32.420 --> 00:20:33.540
He... just now...

00:20:51.340 --> 00:20:52.690
Joshua?

00:20:54.760 --> 00:20:55.890
No way...

00:21:05.740 --> 00:21:09.600
No!

00:22:49.910 --> 00:22:52.850
Hey, Stella! There you are!

00:22:52.850 --> 00:22:55.980
These are all the survivors 
we have, sad to say.

00:23:00.660 --> 00:23:02.760
Special Ensign Gail Owens.

00:23:03.230 --> 00:23:05.690
Their commander died in combat,

00:23:05.690 --> 00:23:09.110
so I'll be taking command of the five 
members of the Buerger Squad.

00:23:09.720 --> 00:23:12.900
Too bad it's such a band of weirdos.

00:23:12.900 --> 00:23:15.030
I daresay I'm the only normal one.

00:23:20.570 --> 00:23:21.710
A pleasure to meet you.

00:23:22.200 --> 00:23:24.350
I am Petty Officer First Class
Stella Shining.

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:40.310
<b><i>The Soldier of Smiles</i></b>
